Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.52,0:00:04.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.44,0:00:05.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.47,0:00:11.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sensei!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.45,0:00:21.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sensei!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.45,0:00:29.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.34,0:00:33.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.85,0:00:35.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.56,0:00:41.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.28,0:00:43.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That right arm of yours \Nis a nuisance.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.85,0:00:50.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to pull off \Nall that useless stuff—
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.19,0:00:52.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,those ugly mechanical parts!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.57,0:00:53.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What did you call them?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.90,0:00:57.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And then I'm going to take \Neverything that is left over.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.99,0:01:00.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, you!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.94,0:01:08.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, you...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.33,0:01:09.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.13,0:01:13.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.06,0:01:18.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.03,0:01:20.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.00,0:01:24.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,you said that homunculi \Ncan't use alchemy, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.64,0:01:27.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But this guy is different.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.07,0:01:29.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've figured out what his secret is.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.91,0:01:33.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When his right arm and left leg form a circle,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.19,0:01:37.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,he can transmute the outside of his body into other materials.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.01,0:01:42.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He can change his body \Nbecause he's a homunculus.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.62,0:01:46.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But he can use alchemy because...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.82,0:01:50.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because he has Ed's limbs \Nin those places?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.30,0:01:52.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My...?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.67,0:01:55.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Give them back! \NThose belong to Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.00,0:01:58.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They are Brother's arm and leg!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.18,0:01:59.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Give them back!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.34,0:02:02.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, you!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.26,0:02:04.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.27,0:02:13.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fine by me!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.11,0:02:14.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.34,0:02:17.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al! Please, stop already!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.61,0:02:22.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you talking about? \NHe's a homunculus. He's not human.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.34,0:02:39.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But still, that boy is Izumi-san's—
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.94,0:02:41.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Maybe so...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.10,0:02:53.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You want my arm, do you?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.90,0:02:55.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's {\i1}my{\i0} arm!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.51,0:03:00.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You gained something for the price of this leg, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.39,0:03:06.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You paid for your brother \Nwith this arm.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.82,0:03:14.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In that case, what are you going to pay to deprive me of my arm and leg?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.95,0:03:17.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,An equivalent exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.84,0:03:19.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop jerking me around!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.43,0:03:21.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.85,0:03:31.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything \Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.60,0:03:36.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to obtain anything, \Nsomething of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.86,0:03:41.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is alchemy's \NLaw of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.59,0:03:47.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that \Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.84,0:05:50.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sensei...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.39,0:05:55.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed! Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.27,0:05:58.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I forbid you to get involved!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.00,0:06:00.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That boy is my sin,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.86,0:06:01.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and I will...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.05,0:06:05.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sensei!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.05,0:06:08.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold it!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.24,0:06:10.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Winry! Take care of Sensei!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.86,0:06:13.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just a minute! Ed! Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.86,0:06:32.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fullmetal Alchemist, I understand this is the island where you did your training.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.73,0:06:34.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, that woman...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.96,0:06:37.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Führer, what are you doing here?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.62,0:06:40.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It appears we are looking for the same thing as you are.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.96,0:06:42.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A homunculus?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.65,0:06:45.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I hear that's what \Nthe enemy calls itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.60,0:06:46.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.96,0:06:53.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,do you guys know how a homunculus is born?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.22,0:07:00.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,According to tradition, it's said that \Na homunculus is the grown-up form
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.50,0:07:04.49,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,of the botched product that is born when someone attempts a human transmutation.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.49,0:07:08.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was written in your \Nfather's research as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.04,0:07:13.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I couldn't care less \Nabout the guy.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.26,0:07:16.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.73,0:07:23.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But if the boy whom Lt. Col. Archer found really is a homunculus,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.11,0:07:26.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that would mean that someone had attempted a human transmutation.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.93,0:07:32.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Human transmutation is impermissible, no matter what the circumstances are.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.15,0:07:34.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you have any idea \Nwho this person might be?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.47,0:07:36.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Never mind that, we should be after the escaped homunculus.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.60,0:07:39.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Our men are already pursuing him.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.83,0:07:43.44,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,I'm sorry, but I don't know. \NWe're in a hurry here, so if you don't mind...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.24,0:07:50.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.49,0:07:53.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We can't tell them \Nabout Sensei, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.18,0:07:54.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Maybe so, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.50,0:07:59.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well? How does it feel, holding him?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.51,0:08:01.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.88,0:08:08.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wrath... That makes all seven of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.16,0:08:10.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After all this time, how about we go to that woman's place?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.89,0:08:14.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Luckily, it's close by, and we do need to tell her about Greed.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.31,0:08:16.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why Greed?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.18,0:08:20.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because long ago, \Nshe's the one who created Greed.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.19,0:08:24.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.77,0:08:28.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why did you show that \Nto my brother?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.81,0:08:32.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The man understood \Neverything I told him.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.83,0:08:37.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What I handed down to him were the ancient memories of the Ishbalan people.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.89,0:08:40.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And as a result, my brother...!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.11,0:08:43.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You must not forget.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.44,0:08:46.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Inside here, they are still alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.20,0:08:49.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Countless lives...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.64,0:08:53.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's here!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.23,0:08:53.76,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,Here he is!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.49,0:09:02.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Due to circumstances beyond our control, we left our established residences.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.45,0:09:06.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As their leader, I will bear full responsibility.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.24,0:09:10.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You do know that new residences have been established here in the south, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.48,0:09:13.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You will all be taken there.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.30,0:09:15.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Make sure that you tell them not to offer any resistance.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.76,0:09:16.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.28,0:09:21.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, before that happens, we will be checking everyone's names and faces.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.15,0:09:22.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Every last one of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.64,0:09:25.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is there someone \Nyou're looking for?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.35,0:09:27.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Begin.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.83,0:09:35.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please, be careful. I'm sure I saw \Nthat homicidal maniac from Central.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.14,0:09:39.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I saw his wanted poster at the home of someone I was taking care of earlier.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.34,0:09:41.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's hope you didn't \Nmistake him for someone else.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.75,0:09:46.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mama!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.33,0:09:46.19,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,All right, you all!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.92,0:09:49.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, where is he?! \NThe man with the X-shaped scar!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.69,0:09:51.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It won't do you \Nany good to hide him!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.34,0:09:55.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's going on here?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.79,0:09:59.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,J-Just you try doing anything against me! \NThe military won't stand for—
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.45,0:10:05.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A-A gunshot?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.88,0:10:07.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I didn't hear any gunfire!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.64,0:10:27.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop! Don't shoot!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.14,0:10:29.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop firing, you stupid bastards!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.11,0:10:37.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Everyone, calm down!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.20,0:10:40.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who was it that \Nacted against this man?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.03,0:10:42.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is the massacre \Ngoing to repeat itself?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.23,0:10:44.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've already had \Ntoo much of this!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.36,0:10:46.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right! How can we \Nkeep silent any longer?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.77,0:10:48.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sick of being under the military's thumb!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.18,0:10:49.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Our people have been killed!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.50,0:10:55.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go back to where \Nyou came from, now!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.13,0:10:56.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah! Get out of here!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.65,0:10:59.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yow!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.65,0:11:03.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to suppress them. \NCover me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.25,0:11:05.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.26,0:11:09.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you waiting for? I told you to cover me!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.88,0:11:12.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And wipe your forehead, would you?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.00,0:11:14.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.57,0:11:28.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good grief. What a pathetic story, both for master and pupil.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.54,0:11:32.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed, Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.77,0:11:34.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Still, I must draw the line somewhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.80,0:11:37.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You are expelled.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.89,0:11:44.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I did not teach you alchemy so that your bodies would end up like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.96,0:11:48.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't want to see any more of \Nyour disgraceful fighting, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.77,0:11:49.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sensei...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.05,0:11:54.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thank you... for taking care of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.88,0:11:58.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please, take care.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.92,0:12:09.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you two sure you just \Nwant to go back home like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.21,0:12:17.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, then...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.35,0:12:20.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. Come by again \Nif you're ever around.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.30,0:12:21.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.08,0:12:24.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She expelled us, and all, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.35,0:12:25.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Foolish bastards!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.47,0:12:28.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now that you are \Nneither master nor pupil,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.96,0:12:32.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it means you can start dealing with each other as equal individuals.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.48,0:12:36.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right! Now, you don't have to feel so constrained by her, do you?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.65,0:12:41.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dammit. Al, we're going back!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.82,0:12:43.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? Mm-hmm!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.37,0:12:45.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't go getting killed.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.46,0:12:52.42,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Sensei! We came here to get some kind of lead as to how to get our original bodies back!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.42,0:12:53.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're not leaving empty-handed!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.89,0:12:55.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Leave!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.14,0:12:56.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're not leaving.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.27,0:12:59.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We want to know the whereabouts of a true Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.85,0:13:02.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,not the one made by \Nsacrificing human lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.40,0:13:03.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Leave.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.20,0:13:04.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're not leaving!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.30,0:13:05.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll cut you up!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.41,0:13:06.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Cut us if you will...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.46,0:13:07.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...but we're not leaving!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.07,0:13:11.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sure that returning that boy over to the other side is...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.75,0:13:13.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is my sin.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.93,0:13:16.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I cannot teach you how to do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.77,0:13:19.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We will take the sin upon ourselves as well!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.06,0:13:29.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You morons...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.11,0:13:36.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You have someone \Nwatching the brothers, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.05,0:13:36.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.14,0:13:40.02,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Don't be caught off guard. \NIf anything happens, let me know immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.02,0:13:40.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.40,0:13:44.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Elric brothers again?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.45,0:13:45.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What choice do we have?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.84,0:13:50.29,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,We received a response from Central that \Nthe Führer did in fact drop by down south here
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.29,0:13:54.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and conducted his own personal investigation into the homunculus.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.06,0:13:56.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Which is exactly the opposite of what they said yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.62,0:14:00.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And with investigations \Npertaining to the homunculi
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.04,0:14:02.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,now under the direct \Nsupervision of the Führer?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.22,0:14:07.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We find out everything the brothers know, like we were originally going to.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.86,0:14:10.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's the possibility that \Nthe Chimera might appear again.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.18,0:14:12.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Kimbly too.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.25,0:14:15.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.74,0:14:37.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is a foul place \Nwe've come to.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.00,0:14:38.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Greed-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.50,0:14:42.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Roa, you guys \Ngo back to Devil's Nest.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.06,0:14:44.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you going off \Nsomeplace by yourself?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.06,0:14:46.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's just something \Nthat's been bothering me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.45,0:14:54.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.97,0:14:58.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, Al, you don't remember anything about the other side of the doorway, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.31,0:14:59.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.75,0:15:03.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If not, then Al's body, \Ntogether with those memories,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.40,0:15:05.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,could still be on the other side.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.26,0:15:08.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How can we get them \Nback from there?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.32,0:15:11.64,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,If we use a Philosopher's Stone, then we can ignore the Principle of Equivalent Exchange
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.64,0:15:13.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and open the doorway once again.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.52,0:15:18.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Equivalent exchange, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.13,0:15:21.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed, do you believe in that?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.07,0:15:23.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Of course he does!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.98,0:15:27.41,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,In order for something to be obtained, it must be accompanied by something of equal value.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.41,0:15:31.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And not just in alchemy, that's a principle throughout the whole world.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.01,0:15:32.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If that's so,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.53,0:15:36.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,then that boy lost his own life before he was ever born.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.48,0:15:40.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And what did he obtain \Nfor that price?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.58,0:15:46.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Apparently, I'm not that good a teacher.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.55,0:15:48.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mason!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.88,0:15:49.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.53,0:15:52.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Show these two where Dante-san's house is.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.35,0:15:55.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Tomorrow, I'll have them \Ngo there to get some medicine.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.47,0:16:00.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Did you think you were \Ngoing to stay here for free?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.77,0:16:04.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wonder what kind of person this Dante-san is.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.88,0:16:09.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A famous pharmacist, \Nfrom what Mason-san said.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.84,0:16:14.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, there's something that's been bothering me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.68,0:16:19.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Supposing that homunculi are born when a human transmutation fails...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.15,0:16:20.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come on, Al, \Nlet's get a move on!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.04,0:16:23.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Anyone home?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.23,0:16:29.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've been expecting you.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.39,0:16:31.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dante-sama is waiting for you inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.67,0:16:32.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.82,0:16:34.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's you!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.54,0:16:39.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lyra?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.54,0:16:39.31,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,Lyra-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.54,0:16:43.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm terribly sorry for what happened on that occasion.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.40,0:16:45.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you doing here?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.75,0:16:49.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am employed here \Nas Dante-sama's pupil,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.52,0:16:53.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so that I may become as superb an alchemist as she is.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.85,0:16:56.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dante-san is an alchemist?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.64,0:16:57.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.62,0:17:00.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is all thanks to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.91,0:17:03.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You taught me something important.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.40,0:17:05.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your character has \Ncompletely changed, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.55,0:17:08.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come in.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.76,0:17:09.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have brought them.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.96,0:17:16.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've been waiting for you, \NElric brothers.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.24,0:17:18.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're Dante-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.10,0:17:22.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes. I was surprised to find that you were Izumi's students.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.32,0:17:27.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've heard what is going on. \NI will get her medicine ready at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.10,0:17:30.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,U-Um, by any chance, did our teacher also...?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.29,0:17:35.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes. Long ago, \Nshe learned alchemy here.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.39,0:17:36.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.61,0:17:37.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.32,0:17:41.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then, Dante-san, that makes you \Nour teacher's teacher!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.35,0:17:43.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I suppose that's what it means.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.68,0:17:49.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, now, how did a guy \Nlike me get to be so lucky?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.57,0:17:53.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And here I just came by to see a familiar face.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.17,0:17:54.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.48,0:17:57.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,there's no letting them out of my sight now.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.22,0:18:00.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you serious about that?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.22,0:18:03.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You {\i1}are{\i0} a fellow State Alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.21,0:18:08.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, we just got word from Greed-san. \NIt sounds like he needs some more hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.81,0:18:12.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please, think it over.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.46,0:18:25.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dante-san, why did you decide to become an alchemist?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.64,0:18:26.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's see...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.19,0:18:28.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It may sound corny,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.85,0:18:32.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but I suppose it was because I wanted to help people.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.42,0:18:35.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alchemy is something \Nthat people need.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.54,0:18:39.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Of course, the alchemy by itself isn't anything all that special.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.22,0:18:42.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But still, when it comes to working to help others,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.08,0:18:44.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that's something \Nthat alchemy can do.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.35,0:18:49.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'd like for people that strive to be happy to be rewarded for as hard as they work.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.72,0:18:51.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's the way I felt.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.53,0:18:52.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Equivalent exchange?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.45,0:18:59.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes. People can only gain one thing for one effort.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.88,0:19:02.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is the absolute truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.30,0:19:10.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dante-san, what do you think \Nabout the Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.02,0:19:13.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you two searching for \Nthe Philosopher's Stone too?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.24,0:19:16.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,N-No, we were...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.33,0:19:19.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All those who have sought the Philosopher's Stone
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.97,0:19:22.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,have been driven to despair.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.55,0:19:27.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It may be that it is too soon for mankind to acquire the Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.38,0:19:32.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You know, you bear \Nsuch a resemblance to him.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.10,0:19:38.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your father, Hohenheim the Light, \Nalso sought the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.34,0:19:40.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Our father did?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.19,0:19:43.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you know \Nwhere your father is?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.62,0:19:45.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't even want to know.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.63,0:19:46.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.85,0:19:59.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They've split up.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.94,0:20:03.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Handle the rest \Nlike we planned.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.01,0:20:04.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Got it?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.23,0:20:05.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.85,0:20:09.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now then...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.03,0:20:20.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You...!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.30,0:20:24.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, you!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.39,0:20:37.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You must be surprised. \NI call it the Mightiest Shield.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.24,0:20:47.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lyra-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.68,0:20:50.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lyra-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.66,0:20:53.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't move!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.10,0:20:57.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As long as you don't resist, \NI have no intention of harming her.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.48,0:20:58.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dante-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.89,0:21:00.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good day.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.35,0:21:04.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who are you folks?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.77,0:21:06.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're kidnappers.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.07,0:21:07.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Kidnappers?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.04,0:21:10.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alphonse Elric,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.36,0:21:12.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, but you'll \Nhave to come with us.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.10,0:21:17.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But Sensei taught me that \NI shouldn't go with strangers.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.82,0:21:20.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you, stupid? Just how old are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.69,0:21:21.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fourteen.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.80,0:21:23.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you're fourteen,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:23.42,0:21:26.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,then you're old enough to think and behave all by yourself, aren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.79,0:21:31.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Listen up. If you're a real man, you'll act on your own will!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.67,0:21:32.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.61,0:21:35.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can't go on forever doing things just because your teacher said to.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.83,0:21:38.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I get it. I have to think for myself, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.38,0:21:39.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Exactly.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.20,0:21:42.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now that you've figured that out, come with us—
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.15,0:21:48.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After thinking about it for myself,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.99,0:21:51.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've decided that I'm not \Ngoing to go with strangers.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.73,0:21:57.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.02,0:23:41.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:41.89,0:23:45.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 33: "Al, Captured"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.36,0:23:49.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have no intention of negotiating with the thugs who have taken my brother!
